@claimBaseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@authBaseUrl = http://localhost:8082

### Scenario 32
### User deactivation publishes an auth event and claim-service closes active claims asynchronously

### 32.1 Create a claim
# @name createClaim
POST {{claimBaseUrl}}/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "landlordUserId": 1,
  "tenantUserId": 3,
  "title": "Deactivation demo claim",
  "description": "This claim should be closed when the tenant is deactivated.",
  "claimedAmount": 70.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 32.2 Deactivate the tenant while the claim is still active
POST {{authBaseUrl}}/api/auth/users/3/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Manual operator deactivation for distributed transaction demo"
}

### 32.3 Poll claim until status becomes CLOSED_NO_PENALTY
GET {{claimBaseUrl}}/api/claims/{{createClaim.response.body.$.id}}

### 32.4 Inspect timeline
GET {{claimBaseUrl}}/api/claims/{{createClaim.response.body.$.id}}/timeline
